IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sa-powers-procedure`

-- Societies Act 1966, ss 26 to 37 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.

§ `Sections 26 to 28 -- entry, search and arrest`

-- s 26: the Registrar, an Assistant Registrar, a Magistrate, or a police officer authorised in writing.
#ASSERT `the person may enter a registered society's place under section 26` `the Registrar`
#ASSERT `the person may enter a registered society's place under section 26` `an Assistant Registrar`
#ASSERT `the person may enter a registered society's place under section 26` `a Magistrate`
#ASSERT `the person may enter a registered society's place under section 26` `a police officer below that rank authorised in writing by the Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a Magistrate`

-- Not a Justice of the Peace, and not a police officer acting on their own motion, however senior.
#ASSERT NOT `the person may enter a registered society's place under section 26` `a Justice of the Peace`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may enter a registered society's place under section 26` `a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may enter a registered society's place under section 26` `a police officer below that rank with no authorisation`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may enter a registered society's place under section 26` `anyone else`

#ASSERT `the person may enter and search under section 27` `the Registrar`
#ASSERT `the person may enter and search under section 27` `a Magistrate`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may enter and search under section 27` `a Justice of the Peace`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may enter and search under section 27` `a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent`

-- s 28 is wider about who: a Justice of the Peace and a senior police officer on their own motion.
#ASSERT `the person may enter and arrest under section 28` `a Magistrate`
#ASSERT `the person may enter and arrest under section 28` `a Justice of the Peace`
#ASSERT `the person may enter and arrest under section 28` `a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent`
#ASSERT `the person may enter and arrest under section 28` `a police officer below that rank authorised in writing by the Registrar, an Assistant Registrar or a Magistrate`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may enter and arrest under section 28` `a police officer below that rank with no authorisation`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may enter and arrest under section 28` `the Registrar`

-- The Registrar can enter and search a registered society's premises under ss 26 and 27, and cannot enter and arrest
-- under s 28.
#ASSERT `the person may enter and search under section 27` `an Assistant Registrar`

-- No warrant is required or mentioned for ss 26 and 27; s 28 is not confined to the persons reasonably suspected,
-- and states no time within which an arrested person must be brought before a court.
#ASSERT NOT `sections 26 and 27 require a warrant`
#ASSERT NOT `section 28 confines the arrest to persons reasonably suspected of involvement`
#ASSERT NOT `section 28 states a time within which an arrested person must be brought before a court`

§ `Sections 29, 29A and 29B -- investigation`

GIVEN `purpose in section 29` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exercised by the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonably believes the person has it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonable period specified` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `person failed to provide` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `might tend to incriminate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `does not possess it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN InvestigationFacts
DECIDE `an investigation` `purpose in section 29` `exercised by the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` `reasonably believes the person has it` `reasonable period specified` `person failed to provide` `person has a reasonable excuse` `might tend to incriminate` `does not possess it` `took all reasonable steps` IS
    InvestigationFacts WITH
        `the purpose is one of the three in section 29` IS `purpose in section 29`
        `the power is exercised by the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar` IS `exercised by the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar`
        `the Registrar reasonably believes the person has the information or thing` IS `reasonably believes the person has it`
        `a reasonable period was specified` IS `reasonable period specified`
        `the person failed to provide or produce` IS `person failed to provide`
        `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS `person has a reasonable excuse`
        `providing it might tend to incriminate the person` IS `might tend to incriminate`
        `the person does not possess the information or thing` IS `does not possess it`
        `the person took all reasonable steps to obtain it and could not` IS `took all reasonable steps`

#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(1)` (`an investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- Each element of a valid requirement is needed.
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(1)` (`an investigation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(1)` (`an investigation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(1)` (`an investigation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(1)` (`an investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(1)` (`an investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- The excuses: a reasonable excuse, self-incrimination, not possessing it, taking all reasonable steps.
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(1)` (`an investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(1)` (`an investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(1)` (`an investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(1)` (`an investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

GIVEN `member of an unlawful society` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused to give information` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave false information` IS A BOOLEAN, `advisable to identify` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN ExaminationFacts
DECIDE `an examination` `member of an unlawful society` `refused to give information` `gave false information` `advisable to identify` IS
    ExaminationFacts WITH
        `satisfied after due inquiry that the person is a member of an unlawful society` IS `member of an unlawful society`
        `satisfied that the person refused to give information about an unlawful or suspected unlawful society` IS `refused to give information`
        `satisfied that the person gave false information about an unlawful or suspected unlawful society` IS `gave false information`
        `the Registrar considers it advisable to identify the person` IS `advisable to identify`

#ASSERT `the Registrar may order a photograph and finger impressions` (`an examination` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may order a photograph and finger impressions` (`an examination` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may order a photograph and finger impressions` (`an examination` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)

-- The Registrar must also think identification advisable.
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may order a photograph and finger impressions` (`an examination` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may order a photograph and finger impressions` (`an examination` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- The privilege protects what would expose the person to a criminal charge, and not a false answer.
#ASSERT `the person is bound to answer under section 29A(4)` (AnswerFacts WITH `the answer would expose the person to a criminal charge, penalty or forfeiture` IS FALSE, `the person gave a false answer` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is bound to answer under section 29A(4)` (AnswerFacts WITH `the answer would expose the person to a criminal charge, penalty or forfeiture` IS TRUE, `the person gave a false answer` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the privilege against self-incrimination excuses a false answer`

#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(2)` (FalseStatementFacts WITH `intentionally altered, suppressed or destroyed what was required` IS TRUE, `made a statement the person knows or ought reasonably to know is, or is reckless as to whether it is, false or misleading in a material particular` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(2)` (FalseStatementFacts WITH `intentionally altered, suppressed or destroyed what was required` IS FALSE, `made a statement the person knows or ought reasonably to know is, or is reckless as to whether it is, false or misleading in a material particular` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person commits the offence in section 29B(2)` (FalseStatementFacts WITH `intentionally altered, suppressed or destroyed what was required` IS FALSE, `made a statement the person knows or ought reasonably to know is, or is reckless as to whether it is, false or misleading in a material particular` IS FALSE)

§ `Sections 30 to 32 -- charging, composing, trying, forfeiting`

-- Anyone arrested under s 28 can be charged without the Registrar's sanction; everyone else needs it.
#ASSERT `the person may be charged` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the person may be charged` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the person may be charged` FALSE FALSE

-- s 30A: half the maximum fine, if prescribed as compoundable.
#ASSERT `the most that may be collected to compound the offence` TRUE 10000 EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `the most that may be collected to compound the offence` TRUE 6000 EQUALS JUST 3000
#ASSERT `the most that may be collected to compound the offence` FALSE 10000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `further proceedings may be taken for the offence` TRUE
#ASSERT `further proceedings may be taken for the offence` FALSE

-- s 31: the five-year offence is a District Court matter only.
#ASSERT NOT `a Magistrate's Court may try the offence` `an offence under section 14(2)`
#ASSERT `a Magistrate's Court may try the offence` `any other offence under the Act or regulations`

#ASSERT NOT `forfeiture under section 32 waits for a conviction`

§ `Section 33 -- service`

#ASSERT `the method is one section 33(3) allows` `giving it to the individual personally`
#ASSERT `the method is one section 33(3) allows` `prepaid registered post`
#ASSERT `the method is one section 33(3) allows` `leaving it with an adult apparently resident or employed at the address`
#ASSERT `the method is one section 33(3) allows` `affixing a copy in a conspicuous place at the address`
#ASSERT `the method is one section 33(3) allows` `email, with the person's prior consent`

-- Email needs prior consent.
#ASSERT NOT `the method is one section 33(3) allows` `email, without the person's consent`
#ASSERT NOT `the method is one section 33(3) allows` `some other method`

-- Registered post takes effect two days after posting, and a returned letter does not stop it.
#ASSERT `the day service by registered post takes effect` 10 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT NOT `return of a posted document undelivered prevents service taking effect`

§ `Section 34(2) -- breach of regulations`

#ASSERT `the most that may be imposed for a regulation breach` 1 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the most that may be imposed for a regulation breach` 2 EQUALS 1100
#ASSERT `the most that may be imposed for a regulation breach` 11 EQUALS 2000

§ `Section 35 -- dissolution by the members, and judgments against the society`

GIVEN `resident members` IS A NUMBER, `voted for dissolution` IS A NUMBER, `specific rules` IS A BOOLEAN, `smaller proportion in the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DissolutionVote
DECIDE `a dissolution vote` `resident members` `voted for dissolution` `specific rules` `smaller proportion in the rules` IS
    DissolutionVote WITH
        `members resident in Singapore for the time being` IS `resident members`
        `of whom voted for dissolution in person or by proxy at a general meeting convened for the purpose` IS `voted for dissolution`
        `the rules make a specific provision about dissolution` IS `specific rules`
        `the rules require a smaller proportion than three-fifths` IS `smaller proportion in the rules`

-- Three-fifths of ALL resident members: 60 of 100.
#ASSERT `three-fifths of the resident members have voted for dissolution` (`a dissolution vote` 100 60 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the society may be dissolved by its members` (`a dissolution vote` 100 60 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `three-fifths of the resident members have voted for dissolution` (`a dissolution vote` 100 59 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the society may be dissolved by its members` (`a dissolution vote` 100 59 FALSE FALSE)

-- Not of those who attend: a unanimous meeting of 20 out of 100 resident members is nowhere near enough.
#ASSERT NOT `the society may be dissolved by its members` (`a dissolution vote` 100 20 FALSE FALSE)

-- A society of 5 resident members: 3 is three-fifths; 2 is not.
#ASSERT `the society may be dissolved by its members` (`a dissolution vote` 5 3 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the society may be dissolved by its members` (`a dissolution vote` 5 2 FALSE FALSE)

-- (g) is the default; (h) is unconditional. A rule allowing dissolution by a smaller vote does not displace (h).
#ASSERT `the default rule in section 35(1)(g) applies` (`a dissolution vote` 100 60 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the default rule in section 35(1)(g) applies` (`a dissolution vote` 100 60 TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the society may be dissolved by its members` (`a dissolution vote` 100 51 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a rule allowing dissolution by a smaller vote is effective` (`a dissolution vote` 100 51 TRUE TRUE)

-- s 35(1)(d): no judgment against an officer or member personally, except under s 36.
#ASSERT `the judgment may be enforced against an officer or member personally` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the judgment may be enforced against an officer or member personally` TRUE FALSE

§ `Section 36 -- security for costs and officers' liability`

GIVEN `society was claimant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `security required` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `security insufficient` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `approved the action` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `became an officer later` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took a reasonable measure` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months since the costs became payable` IS A NUMBER,
      `part unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A CostsFacts
DECIDE `a costs situation` `society was claimant` `security required` `security insufficient` `approved the action` `became an officer later` `took a reasonable measure` `months since the costs became payable` `part unsatisfied` IS
    CostsFacts WITH
        `the society was claimant, or an officer purporting to act for it was` IS `society was claimant`
        `the court required security` IS `security required`
        `the security given was not sufficient to pay the defendant's costs` IS `security insufficient`
        `this person was an officer who approved the institution of the action` IS `approved the action`
        `this person became an officer later` IS `became an officer later`
        `this person took a reasonable measure to seek discontinuance` IS `took a reasonable measure`
        `months since the costs became payable` IS `months since the costs became payable`
        `part of the costs remains unsatisfied after deducting the security` IS `part unsatisfied`

#ASSERT `this person is jointly and severally liable under section 36(2)` (`a costs situation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2 TRUE)

-- The officer who approved the action, and the later officer who did nothing, are liable.
#ASSERT `this person is jointly and severally liable under section 36(2)` (`a costs situation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 2 TRUE)

-- The later officer who tried to stop it is not; nor is an officer who neither approved it nor joined later.
#ASSERT NOT `this person is jointly and severally liable under section 36(2)` (`a costs situation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 2 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `this person is jointly and severally liable under section 36(2)` (`a costs situation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 2 TRUE)

-- Only where security was required AND insufficient, and only for what remains unsatisfied after a month.
#ASSERT NOT `this person is jointly and severally liable under section 36(2)` (`a costs situation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `this person is jointly and severally liable under section 36(2)` (`a costs situation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `this person is jointly and severally liable under section 36(2)` (`a costs situation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 1 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `this person is jointly and severally liable under section 36(2)` (`a costs situation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `this person is jointly and severally liable under section 36(2)` (`a costs situation` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 2 TRUE)

§ `Section 37 -- the power to exempt`

#ASSERT `the Act's provisions are disapplied to the society by section 37` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Act's provisions are disapplied to the society by section 37` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Act's provisions are disapplied to the society by section 37` FALSE TRUE

-- The power is to exempt a REGISTERED society, so it cannot excuse an unregistered group from s 14.
#ASSERT NOT `section 37 can exempt an unregistered society from section 14` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 37 can exempt an unregistered society from section 14` TRUE
